  "unscored": [
    "maps-site/index.html sizes the Leaflet map once at startup (fillZoom() reads map.getSize()), and the header and footer heights depend on which font is showing (iPhone 13 header 111 px on the fallback serif, 116 px with EB Garamond), so the first view depends on whether the web fonts beat the inline script. Fix it so text takes the same boxes before and after the swap; never by re-fitting (a ResizeObserver re-fit fetched both tile grids, 45 tiles, and was rejected) and never by changing which fonts load or when",
    "apply docs/mobile/inputs/A-U0.patch (a measured prototype, CSS only: metric-matched local fallback faces 'EB Garamond fb', 'Lora fb', 'IBM Plex Mono fb' with size-adjust / ascent-, descent-, line-gap-override over the web subsets' unicode-range, each listed right after its web face in every font-family stack, plus header and footer line-heights pinned to the web faces' line boxes for WebKit); change it only if a check below fails, and say why",
    "with the fonts blocked and with them served, on all five profiles: header heights equal (116/116/97/52/52 px for iphone13/pixel7/landscape/desktop/desktop2x), footers equal, and map.getSize() equals the #map box (390x509, 412x698, 844x215, 1366x688, 1440x820); no JS change, no new clock token, no matchMedia, no timer, the canvas font string unchanged",
    "the header, controls, company bar, scale bar and footer pixels unchanged (the shots outside the map raster)",
    "header_h and the chrome controls NOT declared (they must equal the reference)",
    "two captures of the edited tree give identical iphone13 atlas keys; the WebKit and Android notes in the patch's comment hold (no WebKit browser here: Mobile 15's real-device pass checks iOS and Android)"
  ]
